Hyphenation patterns
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

mw-core/src/main/resources/hyphenation/ holds two pattern files taken verbatim
from the hyph-utf8 project (http://www.hyphenation.org/tex), used to split lyric
words into syllables. They are data, not code, and each carries its own terms.

hyph-it.pat.txt -- Italian
  Copyright (C) 2008-2011 Claudio Beccari
  Available under any of several licences, of which this project takes the MIT
  one. (The copies distributed with Apache FOP are LPPL-only: that conversion
  predates the relicensing, which is why these are taken from the source.)

hyph-en-us.pat.txt -- American English
  Copyright (C) 1990, 2004, 2005 Gerard D.C. Kuiken
  "Copying and distribution of this file, with or without modification, are
  permitted in any medium without royalty provided the copyright notice and
  this notice are preserved."

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
External tools
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PDF engraving is performed by invoking LilyPond (GPL-3.0) as a separate
process. LilyPond is not linked, bundled or redistributed with this software,
and the program functions without it (emitting LilyPond, MusicXML and MIDI
sources instead).
